From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: let legacy GEM close exit after terminal GPU failure

Source: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/fdf3c8b8b912022ef6f01538cc5e4c943459c93b
Applies after liuqin 7.3.1 refresh/0019; upstream logic retained.
Validation and rollback: tasks/upstream-refresh/RESULT.md.

msm_gem_close waits uninterruptibly for BOOKKEEP fences with no deadline.
When failed recovery cannot confirm that DMA has stopped, its fences
must remain pending for memory safety. Closing a handle or exiting the
client then blocks forever, even with SIGKILL pending.

Wait interruptibly and recheck the terminal GPU state once per second.
On termination or a signal, retain the mapping for final GEM object
cleanup rather than releasing memory that hardware may still access.
Pending submits retain the BO, vm_bo and context references. This does
not impose a deadline on DMA, pretend that a fence completed, or signal
any fence belonging to another producer. Normal completed work retains
the existing immediate mapping teardown.

This extends the safe-quiescence policy of 018982b5e1ac from
linux-sm8450-liuqin. The legacy close path is shared by Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro,
OnePlus Pad 2 Pro and Xiaomi Pad 6 Pro. VM_BIND uses a different teardown
path and is not changed by this patch.

Fixes: cefb919cfa53 ("drm/msm: Use DMA_RESV_USAGE_BOOKKEEP/KERNEL")
Link: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/018982b5e1ac830617c6aed9cacb6cc68f4eae1a
Co-Authored-By: gpt-6-astra <noreply@openai.com>

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
@@ -49,8 +49,10 @@ static void put_iova_spaces(struct drm_gem_object *obj, struct drm_gpuvm *vm,
 
 static void msm_gem_close(struct drm_gem_object *obj, struct drm_file *file)
 {
+	struct msm_drm_private *priv = obj->dev->dev_private;
 	struct msm_context *ctx = file->driver_priv;
 	struct drm_exec exec;
+	long ret;
 
 	update_ctx_mem(file, -obj->size);
 	msm_gem_vma_put(obj);
@@ -72,11 +74,23 @@ static void msm_gem_close(struct drm_gem_object *obj, struct drm_file *file)
 		return;
 
 	/*
-	 * TODO we might need to kick this to a queue to avoid blocking
-	 * in CLOSE ioctl
+	 * Recovery may be unable to stop DMA. In that case it must retain
+	 * pending fences and BO references, but close must still let the
+	 * process exit. Leave the mappings to msm_gem_free_object() instead
+	 * of unmapping memory that the GPU might still access. The same is
+	 * safe if a signal interrupts the wait: submits hold the BO and VM.
+	 *
+	 * Recheck the terminal state once a second; this is not a deadline
+	 * for releasing buffers or for completing externally owned fences.
 	 */
-	dma_resv_wait_timeout(obj->resv, DMA_RESV_USAGE_BOOKKEEP, false,
-			      MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT);
+	while (!dma_resv_test_signaled(obj->resv, DMA_RESV_USAGE_BOOKKEEP)) {
+		if (READ_ONCE(priv->gpu->wedged))
+			return;
+		ret = dma_resv_wait_timeout(obj->resv, DMA_RESV_USAGE_BOOKKEEP,
+					    true, HZ);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return;
+	}
 
 	msm_gem_lock_vm_and_obj(&exec, obj, ctx->vm);
 	put_iova_spaces(obj, ctx->vm, true, "close");
